    <section class="mt-10">
      <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Readonly mode</h3>
      <p class="mb-5 text-sm text-base-content/60">
        Unlike the other three views, this one does not freeze its control — it drops the textarea and renders the
        submitted text instead. A disabled textarea would leave a long answer stranded behind a scrollbar the
        student can no longer drag, which is the opposite of what a frozen view is for. Each <code
          class="font-mono">input</code
        > kind is displayed the way it was meant to be read: Markdown rendered, code in a code mockup, plain text
        with its whitespace intact. An answer nobody wrote says so, rather than showing an empty box.
      </p>
