      <p class="mb-5 text-sm text-base-content/60">
        One box, shaped by the question's <code class="font-mono">domain</code> — resolved by{" "}
        <code class="font-mono">toPublic()</code>, so the view never reimplements mdq.spec's coercion table. An{" "}
        <code class="font-mono">integer</code> or <code class="font-mono">decimal</code> question gets a number
        input stepped by <code class="font-mono">decimalPlaces</code>; a <code class="font-mono">fraction</code>
        {" "}question gets a text input, because a number input rejects <code class="font-mono">1/3</code> outright
        and a domain nobody can type in is not a domain. <code class="font-mono">unit</code> is a label on the box
        and nothing more — no unit conversion is performed.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <Card title="Integer, with a unit">
          <NumericView client:load question={water.toPublic()} mode="answer" />
