    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h3 class="mb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Review mode</h3>
      <p class="mb-5 text-sm text-base-content/60">
        Grading is binary: 998 g is inside the question's 5 g tolerance and scores 1, and 100 g scores 0. There is
        no partial credit for being close — the tolerance is the only notion of closeness mdq.spec has. The check
        and the x are read off <code class="font-mono">result.score</code>, not derived from the key, because the
        tolerance that decides them is not public. They show even on the last card, where the expected value is
        withheld: with one box and a score badge beside it, hiding the check would conceal nothing.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <Card title="Inside the tolerance">
